            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Could this issue be reopened? Deleting a terminal buffer immediately after chansend() hangs Neovim with the standalone reproduction below. The backtrace appears consistent with the cleanup loop described here.\n\n## Environment\n\nReproduced on Linux with:\n\n- Neovim 0.12.6\n- Neovim 0.13.0-dev-1805+g39a740aaa7\n\nNo plugins or user configuration are required.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nSave as repro.lua:\n\n```lua\n  local job = vim.fn.jobstart({\n    '/bin/sh', '-c', 'printf \"ready\\\\n\"; exec cat',\n  }, { term = true })\n\n  assert(job > 0)\n  assert(vim.wait(1000, function()\n    return vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, 0, 1, false)[1] == 'ready'\n  end))\n\n  -- Write and delete before libuv completes the write.\n  vim.fn.chansend(job, 'pending write\\n')\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(0, { force = true })\n\n  -- Process queued events immediately after deletion.\n  vim.wait(1, function() return false end)\n\n  io.stdout:write('terminal deletion completed\\n')\n  vim.cmd('qa!')\n```\n\nRun with an external timeout; vim.wait() does not return during the hang:\n\n```sh\n  timeout -k 1s 3s nvim --headless -u NONE -i NONE \\\n    --noplugin -n -l repro.lua\n```\n\nExpected: prints terminal deletion completed and exits.\n\nActual: prints nothing and hangs until forcibly killed. This occurred in all three attempts on each unpatched build.\n\n## Investigation\n\nInterrupting the development build in a debugger produced this stack:\n\n```text\n  multiqueue_put_event\n  term_delayed_free\n  multiqueue_process_events\n  nlua_loop_poll\n```\n\nterm_delayed_free requeues itself onto chan->events while terminal I/O remains pending. The event processor keeps draining that queue, preventing libuv from running the callback that clears the pending write.\n\nThe same retry remains in upstream channel.c at d714648b8e7c.\n\n## Candidate fix\n\nThe local change is:\n\n```diff\n  -    multiqueue_put(chan->events, term_delayed_free, chan);\n  +    loop_schedule_deferred(&main_loop, event_create(term_delayed_free, chan));\n```\n\nThe local patched build completed the reproduction in all three attempts, taking 27–29 ms.\n\nThis appears to let libuv make progress before cleanup retries. The pending-I/O checks and explicit reference-count operations are unchanged, but shutdown behavior, event ordering, and cross-platform safety still need validation.\n\nPR #32755 addressed similar same-queue rescheduling in emit_termrequest; this reproduction reaches the separate cleanup path in channel.c.\n",
